    <title>05 | 人类是如何被人工智能改变的？从传播学出发的跨学科对话</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/62ea9ac2d1df4a5f44efbc51</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">62ea9ac2d1df4a5f44efbc51</guid>
    <pubDate>Thu, 04 Aug 2022 02:30:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>大家好，我是Eve，今天是新传自习室的第五期节目。今天我们讨论的话题是：</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>人类是如何被人工智能改变的？从传播学出发的跨学科对话</span></strong></p><span></span><p><span>人工智能已经成为了过去十年间最火热的话题和进展最快的研究领域之一。当计算机学者和从业者着力于提升人工智能的能力和智慧，一些社会科学和人类学家则关注着人类在人工智能产业中正扮演着什么样的角色，又是如何被改变。</span></p><span></span><p><span>我们请到了拥有不同学科背景的学者，从他们的工作出发，讨论人类与人工智能的关系。今年五月，段泽宁</span><a href="https://academic.oup.com/hcr/article/48/3/516/6587151" data-url="https://academic.oup.com/hcr/article/48/3/516/6587151"><span>关于社交机器人的研究</span></a><span>发布于Human Communication Research，讨论了推特机器人如何回应人类和媒体的内容生产。七月，</span><a href="https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/scirobotics.abm4183" data-url="https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/scirobotics.abm4183"><span>Leo的一篇关于人机双向价值对齐的研究</span></a><span>发布于Science Robotics，论文内容被一些媒体形容为“机器人拥有人类价值观”。另一位嘉宾蓝熊则关注残障群体与技术的互动，以及他们如何被卷入人工智能产业中。</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>来聊天的朋友们有：</span></strong></p><span></span><p><span>段泽宁🌈： 微博 @段泽宁一梦如是</span></p><span></span><p><span>威斯康星大学麦迪逊分校新闻与大众传播学院博士生，研究工作关注媒介算法、公共舆论和计算社会科学方法。</span></p><span></span><p><span>蓝熊：</span></p><span></span><p><span>从华南流浪到德国和美国的人类学门外汉，关注手语、残障倡导与无障碍未来</span></p><span></span><p><span>Leo♣️: Instagram: yuanluya</span></p><span></span><p><span>博士毕业于加州大学洛杉矶分校计算机科学系人工智能专业, 研究方向为人机和多智能体协作，现在Meta Reality Lab任职Research Scientist</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="479">7:59</a> &nbsp;什么是人工智能体的“价值观”？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="600">10:00</a> 残障者的职业和生活是如何被人工智能产业改变的？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1037">17:17</a> 是谁在做数据标注工作？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1296">21:36</a> “为盲人读书”为什么是一个无效的公益活动？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1587">26:27</a> 人工智能开发者会如何考虑伦理问题？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1962">32:42</a> 大企业的精密分工是否会让企业离用户更远？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2082">34:42</a> 科技企业的技术团队和审核团队是如何协作和制衡的？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2384">39:44</a> 语言专业是否会被人工智能替代？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2707">45:07</a> 聋人社区为什么抵制手语手套？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3460">57:40</a> 社交机器人真的会影响舆论吗？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3577">59:37</a> 公共舆论很廉价，但威力巨大</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="3797">63:17</a> 社交机器人会让社会更不公平吗？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4159">69:19</a> 社交机器人与审核系统的拉锯是永无止境的竞赛</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4332">72:12</a> 水军公司是怎么想的？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4570">76:10</a> 社交机器人的雇佣者是用什么方法左右舆论的？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4602">76:42</a> 社交机器人是否会加深人类之间的偏见？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="4912">81:52</a> 无人驾驶车将会如何解决电车难题？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="5185">86:25</a> 理想中的AI Being应该具有什么样的道德？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="5290">88:10</a> 公众对技术的恐慌，实际上来源于对人的恐慌</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="5474">91:14</a> 开发者“不关心”人工智能是否有自我意识？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="5745">95:45</a> 推荐书目</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>推荐书目</span></strong></p><span></span><p><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=2oy3OXYAAAAJ&amp;hl=zh-CN" data-url="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=2oy3OXYAAAAJ&amp;hl=zh-CN"><span>Steward Russell</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://yalebooks.yale.edu/book/9780300264630/atlas-of-ai/" data-url="https://yalebooks.yale.edu/book/9780300264630/atlas-of-ai/"><span>The Atlas of AI: Power, Politics, and the Planetary Costs of Artificial Intelligence</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>by </span><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kate_Crawford" data-url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kate_Crawford"><span>Kate Crawford</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.dukeupress.edu/spaceship-in-the-desert" data-url="https://www.dukeupress.edu/spaceship-in-the-desert"><span>Spaceship In the Desert: Energy, Climate Change, and Urban Design in Abu Dhabi</span></a></p><span></span><p><span>by </span><a href="https://www.dukeupress.edu/explore-subjects/browse?AuID=1336577" data-url="https://www.dukeupress.edu/explore-subjects/browse?AuID=1336577"><span>Gökçe Günel</span></a></p><span></span><p><strong><span>参考资料</span></strong></p><span></span><p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_gap_hypothesis" data-url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_gap_hypothesis"><span>Knowledge gap hypothesis</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="http://www.npc.gov.cn/zgrdw/npc/xinwen/2018-11/05/content_2065632.htm" data-url="http://www.npc.gov.cn/zgrdw/npc/xinwen/2018-11/05/content_2065632.htm"><span>中华人民共和国残疾人保障法</span></a><span>.</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.ada.gov/2010_regs.htm" data-url="https://www.ada.gov/2010_regs.htm"><span>美国残疾人法案</span></a><span>.</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.science.org/doi/full/10.1126/scirobotics.abm4183?casa_token=BSaOnil4zi4AAAAA%3ATkPw1fGIJ9B6Qwv38sQcxnE3s7zBUxlOb6c3YxyL6iLx-GNo9TkMKVWNcOXolQt2lOL318jv0GiG1A" data-url="https://www.science.org/doi/full/10.1126/scirobotics.abm4183?casa_token=BSaOnil4zi4AAAAA%3ATkPw1fGIJ9B6Qwv38sQcxnE3s7zBUxlOb6c3YxyL6iLx-GNo9TkMKVWNcOXolQt2lOL318jv0GiG1A"><span>Yuan, L., Gao, X., Zheng, Z., Edmonds, M., Wu, Y. N., Rossano, F., ... &amp; Zhu, S. C. (2022). In situ bidirectional human-robot value alignment. Science Robotics, 7(68), eabm4183.</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://academic.oup.com/hcr/article/48/3/516/6587151" data-url="https://academic.oup.com/hcr/article/48/3/516/6587151"><span>Algorithmic Agents in the Hybrid Media System: Social Bots, Selective Amplification, and Partisan News about COVID-19</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://academic.oup.com/hcr/article/48/3/379/6620825?login=true" data-url="https://academic.oup.com/hcr/article/48/3/379/6620825?login=true"><span>Sundar, S. S., &amp; Lee, E. J. (2022). Rethinking Communication in the Era of Artificial Intelligence. Human Communication Research, 48(3), 379-385.</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://academic.oup.com/jcmc/article/25/1/89/5714020" data-url="https://academic.oup.com/jcmc/article/25/1/89/5714020"><span>Hancock, J. T., Naaman, M., &amp; Levy, K. (2020). AI-mediated communication: Definition, research agenda, and ethical considerations. Journal of Computer-Mediated Communication, 25(1), 89-100.</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://academic.oup.com/jcmc/article-abstract/25/1/74/5700811?redirectedFrom=fulltext" data-url="https://academic.oup.com/jcmc/article-abstract/25/1/74/5700811?redirectedFrom=fulltext"><span>Sundar, S. S. (2020). Rise of machine agency: A framework for studying the psychology of human–AI interaction (HAII). Journal of Computer-Mediated Communication, 25(1), 74-88.</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.sohu.com/a/286960085_672100" data-url="https://www.sohu.com/a/286960085_672100"><span>姚登峰，郭晓斌，江铭虎（2019.01.15）前路漫漫 未来可期——走出手语识别的“误区”</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/OBytiM9vhGh_bquX_QNSrg" data-url="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/OBytiM9vhGh_bquX_QNSrg"><span>IT时报（2020.08.31）如果你知道，智能音箱是他们在训练……</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://medium.datadriveninvestor.com/sidewalk-toronto-and-why-smarter-is-not-better-b233058d01c8" data-url="https://medium.datadriveninvestor.com/sidewalk-toronto-and-why-smarter-is-not-better-b233058d01c8"><span>Jutta Treviranus (2017.10.30) Sidewalk Toronto and Why Smarter Is Not Better.&nbsp;</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/tK2nHRsxi1-IOBpQ1PjGaw" data-url="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/tK2nHRsxi1-IOBpQ1PjGaw"><span>甲子光年（2018.02.14）“数据折叠”：今天，那些人工智能背后“标数据的人”正在回家</span></a><span>.</span></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2017/11/why-sign-language-gloves-dont-help-deaf-people/545441/" data-url="https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2017/11/why-sign-language-gloves-dont-help-deaf-people/545441/"><span>Michael Erard （2017.11.9）Why Sign-Language Gloves Don't Help Deaf People.&nbsp;</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://m.weibo.cn/detail/3751768040868948" data-url="https://m.weibo.cn/detail/3751768040868948"><span>一加一残障人有人文化（2014.09.05）为盲胞读书,我忍你很久了.&nbsp;</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/enKkUcc6ELd44kMFbKszxw" data-url="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/enKkUcc6ELd44kMFbKszxw"><span>结绳志（2022.07.27） 一份残障组织与媒体清单.&nbsp;</span></a></p><span></span><p><strong><span>配乐：</span></strong></p><span></span><p><a href="https://elements.envato.com/" data-url="https://elements.envato.com/"><span>envato</span></a></p><span></span><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gA03iyI3yEA" data-url="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gA03iyI3yEA"><span>On the edge by AIVA</span></a></p><span></span><p><strong><span>关于我们</span></strong></p><span></span><p><span>🧣：新传自习室</span></p><span></span><p><span>小宇宙 ｜ 苹果Podcast | Spotify</span></p>]]></description>
